### Personal Fabrication & Minimum-Order-Quantity Exception (Hobbyist PCB Fab Exception)
As a narrow exception solely to allow hobbyists to deal with PCB manufacturer minimum order quantities:
1. You **are permitted** to upload the production files (Gerbers/BOM) to a third-party PCB fabrication service (e.g., JLCPCB, PCBWay, OSHPark, Eurocircuits) solely to manufacture prototypes for your own personal use.
2. Where a PCB manufacturer enforces a Minimum Order Quantity (e.g., a minimum batch of 5 or 10 bare PCBs), you **are permitted** to transfer the surplus **bare (unpopulated) PCBs** to other hobbyists **strictly at documented out-of-pocket cost** (unit PCB cost + customs/taxes + actual shipping, with **zero profit margin**) up to a maximum of **10 bare PCBs per person per year**.
3. This exception **never applies** to the sale of assembled boards, component kits, or recurring listings on e-commerce platforms.

